            "bug_id": 19246,
            "text": "Created attachment 3948\nFix .resetSubclasses to check the correct class union\n\n`.recacheSubclasses()` has:\n\n```\nelse if(is.na(match(what, names(subDef@contains)))) {\n```\n\nBut `what` is also derived from a subclass, so it's _always_ `TRUE`. This has the following observable defects:\n\n```\nsetClassUnion(\"U1\", c(\"factor\", \"numeric\"))\nsetClassUnion(\"U2\", c(\"numeric\", \"factor\"))\nsetGeneric(\"fU\", function(x) standardGeneric(\"fU\"))\nsetMethod(\"fU\", \"U1\", function(x) \"U1\")\nsetMethod(\"fU\", \"numeric\", function(x) \"numeric\")\n\ngetClassDef(\"ordered\")@contains[[\"U1\"]]@distance\n# 4; should be 2. ditto for \"U2\"\n\nfU(ordered(\"a\"))\n# numeric; should be U1, at lower @distance\n```\n\nActual package bugs discovered:\n\n```\nlibrary(kernlab)\nkm <- as.kernelMatrix(matrix(1:4, 2, 2))\nclass(as(km, \"listI\"))\n# [1] integer\n```\n\nBUT kernlab defines (kernlab/R/aobjects.R)\n\n```\nsetClassUnion(\"listI\", c(\"list\", \"numeric\", \"vector\", \"integer\", \"matrix\"))\n```\n\nSo the correct output here is to pick up the matrix->listI path (not matrix->array->structure->vector->listI)\n\nA different one from Matrix:\n\n```\nlibrary(Matrix)\nM <- as(Matrix(c(1, 0.5, 0.5, 1), 2, 2), \"corMatrix\")\nM@sd <- c(2, 3)\nV <- Matrix(c(1, 0.2, 0.2, 1), 2, 2)\n\nsetClassUnion(\"dMatrixOrMatrix\", members = c(\"dMatrix\", \"matrix\"))\nas(M, \"dMatrix\") <- V\nM@sd\n# [1] 1 1\n```\n\nHere, the wrong `@replace` method got picked up, and `@sd` got recomputed instead of copied over.\n\n---\n\nThis was again picked up while trying to improve package load efficiency. The loop always evaluating to `TRUE` causes unnecessary work. c.f.\n\n```\ne <- new.env(parent = .GlobalEnv)\nmembers <- paste0(\"Base_\", 1:40)\nfor (m in members) {\n  setClass(m, where = e)\n  for (s in 1:10) setClass(paste0(m, \"_sub_\", s), contains = m, where = e)\n}\n\nsystem.time(setClassUnion(\"BigUnion\", members, where = e))\n\nu_def <- getClassDef(\"BigUnion\", where = e)\nsystem.time(for (i in 1:100) methods:::.recacheSubclasses(\"BigUnion\", u_def, e))\n\n# BEFORE patch\n#    user  system elapsed \n#   1.501   0.008   1.509 \n#    user  system elapsed \n#   2.216   0.000   2.217\n\n# AFTER patch\n#    user  system elapsed \n#   0.966   0.000   0.966 \n#    user  system elapsed \n#   0.153   0.000   0.153 \n```",
            "creation_time": "2026-10-24T16:54:10Z",
